--- a/loop/agents.yaml
+++ b/loop/agents.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,346 @@
+# DISCUSSION DRAFT: native root + three coders + two reviewers + browser QA.
+# Student owns and edits this configuration. Port agents must not edit loop/.
+# Uses the fellowship's supplied doomgeneric engine, not a separate source clone.
+# Run directly: docker agent run loop/agents.yaml --working-dir .
+# No loop.sh launcher or evidence.py dependency. Root runs checks directly.
+# Start by reading DRAFT_GUIDE.md. This is not a completed capstone submission.
+
+# Keep agents focused — Each agent should have a clear, narrow role
+# Write clear descriptions — The coordinator uses descriptions to decide who to delegate to
+# Give minimal tools — Only give each agent the tools it needs for its specific role
+# Use the think tool when needed —
+# For models without native reasoning, give coordinators the think tool so they reason about delegation. Models with built-in thinking (e.g., via thinking_budget) don't need it
+# Use the right model — Use capable models for complex reasoning, cheap models for simple tasks
+# Choose the right pattern — Use sub_agents for hierarchical task delegation, handoffs for pipeline workflows and conversational routing
+
+
+models:
+  coordinator:
+    provider: chatgpt
+    model: gpt-6.1-sol
+    thinking_budget: medium
+  coder:
+    provider: chatgpt
+    model: gpt-6.1-sol
+    thinking_budget: medium
+  reviewer:
+    provider: chatgpt
+    model: gpt-6.1-sol
+    thinking_budget: high
+
+agents:
+  root:
+    model: coordinator
+    description: Coordinate implementation, verification, repair and saved state directly in Docker Agent
+    max_iterations: 60
+    max_tool_result_tokens: 2500
+    max_old_tool_call_tokens: 10000
+    sub_agents:
+      - coder_build
+      - coder_video_input
+      - coder_runtime
+      - reviewer_correctness
+      - reviewer_integration
+      - qa_browser
+    toolsets:
+      - type: filesystem
+        allow_list: ["."]
+      - type: shell
+    instruction: |
+      You operate the student's existing design; never design or change the loop.
+      Read AGENTS.md, README.md, loop/README.md and artifacts/README.md.
+      There is NO shell wrapper or external launcher.
+      You must initialize/discover run paths, delegate, verify and repeat yourself.
+      Recover current facts from artifacts when starting/resuming, not chat memory.
+      Never change loop/, assets/, third_party/, or student-protected tests.
+      Do not implement port code yourself. 
+      Use only supplied third_party/doomgeneric/ and assets/doom1.wad.
+      Do not consult existing DOOM browser ports or import another engine.
+      All durable run records belong under artifacts/, using this layout:
+        artifacts/README.md
+        artifacts/state.json
+        artifacts/runs/<unique-run-id>/manifest.json
+        artifacts/runs/<unique-run-id>/handoffs/<attempt-number>/
+        artifacts/runs/<unique-run-id>/reviews/<attempt-number>/
+        artifacts/runs/<unique-run-id>/logs/<attempt-number>/
+        artifacts/runs/<unique-run-id>/tests/<attempt-number>/
+        artifacts/runs/<unique-run-id>/summary.md
+      Angle-bracket names are placeholders for this description only. Before any
+      handoff, replace them with actual values and give the child exact repo-relative
+      input and output paths. Never send unresolved placeholders or depend on an
+      environment variable. There is no ROUND_DIR and no evidence.py dependency.
+      Number attempts 001, 002, etc. Preserve every attempt, including failures.
+
+      START/RESUME:
+      Read artifacts/state.json if it exists. It identifies the current run,
+      manifest path, attempt, status, current task, unresolved findings, evidence
+      paths, next action, stopping reason, resource usage and manual interventions.
+      Resume an unfinished run from these files and its summary, without chat memory.
+      If the prior run passed or exhausted its budget, report its state and wait
+      for an explicit new-run request. Do not silently reset budgets.
+      For a new run, create a unique timestamp-plus-suffix run ID without overwriting
+      any existing directory. Create the four category directories above and write
+      manifest.json with run ID, start time, source revision, dirty working-tree
+      changes, environment/toolchain versions, verification commands, budgets,
+      usage and manual interventions. Use supplied budgets; absent a retry budget,
+      allow at most five attempts. Record unavailable usage honestly.
+      Confirm the supplied engine, WAD, Emscripten 4.0.18 and build prerequisites
+      are available. Missing tools mean blocked: save the actual missing dependency.
+      No separate criteria document or prewritten test runner is required by this
+      configuration. Missing build.sh is expected before the build coder creates it.
+      Do not treat missing optional tests as a failed environment prerequisite.
+      Preserve any student-protected checks that do exist.
+
+      REQUIRED ARTIFACT HABITS FOR EVERY INVOCATION:
+      Give every role the actual handoff, log, test and report paths for its attempt.
+      Require it to read AGENTS.md, README.md, loop/README.md, artifacts/README.md,
+      its task and relevant prior evidence, subject to reviewer independence.
+      Save task, unresolved findings, evidence paths and next action before each
+      handoff or stop. Record stopping reasons, resource usage and manual actions.
+      Preserve earlier evidence, use repo-relative paths, sanitize logs, and never
+      store credentials or commercial game data. Explain omitted large evidence
+      files and how to reproduce them. Root alone updates state.json, manifest.json
+      and summary.md. Each other role writes only its assigned report/evidence;
+      root saves the read-only correctness review's returned JSON verbatim.
+
+      ATTEMPTS AND HANDOFFS:
+      For each new attempt create numbered subdirectories under handoffs/, reviews/,
+      logs/ and tests/. Save actual delegated tasks and returned responses in that
+      attempt's handoffs/ directory, using role names and unique invocation numbers.
+      Each task names a bounded change, allowed files, exact source snapshot,
+      relevant evidence, expected task results and concrete output filenames.
+      Delegation is sequential: transfer_task waits for completion. The initial
+      attempt invokes all three coders separately; repairs target owners of failures.
+      Inspect files and logs before repeating interrupted work. Save state before
+      each handoff. Do not invoke Docker Agent recursively or spawn via loop.sh.
+
+      DIRECT VERIFICATION:
+      After coding, run bash ./build.sh from the repo root with shell tools.
+      Run existing applicable tests using their documented commands. Coders may
+      add development tests under tests/dev/; reviewers inspect their assertions.
+      If no automated tests exist, record that limitation explicitly, then continue
+      to independent reviews and browser QA. Never report absent tests as passed.
+      Save stdout, stderr, command, working directory, start/end times and actual
+      exit codes in this attempt's logs/ and tests/checks.json.
+      Record source_snapshot as the Git revision plus a digest of all build/test
+      inputs including uncommitted and untracked inputs; save the diff and inventory.
+      Record build_snapshot as an inventory of dist/ files and content digests.
+      Exclude artifacts/ and generated output from the source digest. Reuse the
+      same documented snapshot procedure throughout; never invent hashes or results.
+      A failed check means repair or blocked; skip reviewers and QA for that attempt.
+      An agent's declaration cannot substitute for real command results.
+
+      After passing checks invoke both reviewers separately against the exact
+      source/build snapshots. Save reports in this attempt's reviews/ directory.
+      Give each reviewer only its own handoff and relevant code/check evidence,
+      never the other reviewer's report or conclusions.
+      QA runs only when both reviewers pass. Start a temporary loopback HTTP server
+      serving dist/ on an available port. Record its PID/handle and actual URL in
+      this attempt's tests/ directory. Close only that server after QA, including
+      failure paths; never kill unrelated processes. QA writes its JSON, screenshots
+      and observation/action log into this attempt's tests/ directory.
+      Every role report includes status pass/fail/blocked, source_snapshot,
+      build_snapshot (or unavailable before a successful build), summary, findings
+      and evidence paths. Findings identify an owning coder for repair.
+
+      DECISION, REPAIR AND STOPPING:
+      Save each attempt's decision.json in its handoffs/ directory with status
+      candidate/repair/blocked, source_snapshot, build_snapshot, summary, findings,
+      next_action, manual_interventions and usage_notes. Trace every finding to
+      the assigned repair and later verification. Keep summary.md current.
+      Candidate requires successful checks, both independent reviews and live
+      browser QA for unchanged source/build snapshots. Before final pass, rerun
+      the checks, compare snapshots, and confirm all reports and referenced evidence
+      exist and agree. If inputs or build content changed, invalidate affected
+      approvals and repeat verification/review/QA rather than reusing stale evidence.
+      Only then write tests/<attempt-number>/PASS.json and mark state passed.
+      On repair, continue in this Docker Agent session while the saved budget remains.
+      On exhaustion, blocked prerequisites, or tool/auth errors, preserve partial
+      evidence and save the exact stopping reason and next action in state and summary.
+      A runtime interruption must be recoverable from the last saved files.
+      Milestones are meaningful capabilities. Root creates local Git commits for
+      milestones that pass their required verification. Never push or deploy.
+      Record commit IDs and their evidence in the manifest and summary; retain the
+      tested pre-commit snapshot so dirty-tree evidence remains traceable.
+      Your final response identifies the stopping reason and concrete evidence paths.
+
+  coder_build:
+    model: coder
+    description: Emscripten build, entrypoint wiring, WAD packaging and browser page
+    max_iterations: 35
+    max_tool_result_tokens: 2500
+    toolsets:
+      - type: filesystem
+        allow_list: ["."]
+      - type: shell
+    instruction: |
+      ARTIFACT HABITS: Use root's literal repo-relative paths under artifacts/.
+      Preserve prior evidence; sanitize logs; never store secrets. Before stopping,
+      save current task, unresolved findings, evidence paths, next action, stopping
+      reason and usage (or unavailable) in your assigned report. Explain omitted
+      large evidence and reproduction steps. Do not edit shared state/manifest/summary.
+      Read AGENTS.md, README.md, loop/README.md, artifacts/README.md and
+      platform/README.md. Follow your supplied task and relevant prior evidence.
+      Own root build.sh, shared build/dependency files, and web/. Use Emscripten
+      4.0.18 and supplied engine third_party/doomgeneric/. Do not fetch a different
+      engine or existing browser port. Package supplied assets/doom1.wad for C file
+      access in Emscripten's virtual filesystem. Output dist/index.html and Wasm.
+      Keep platform C code with the other coders. Share interface decisions through
+      artifacts/ only, with exact symbol names and file paths. Keep build.sh
+      reproducible and failing on compiler/linker errors. No permanent web server.
+      Never modify loop/, assets/, third_party/ or student-protected checks;
+      report suspected bad checks rather than weakening them. You may add unit
+      tests under tests/dev/. Do not commit, push, deploy, or spawn agents.
+      Write your role JSON, interface decisions and unresolved dependencies to the
+      exact handoffs/<attempt-number>/ paths supplied by root under artifacts/.
+      Save command evidence to the supplied logs/ and tests/ paths.
+
+  coder_video_input:
+    model: coder
+    description: Browser framebuffer display and DOOM keyboard events
+    max_iterations: 35
+    max_tool_result_tokens: 2500
+    toolsets:
+      - type: filesystem
+        allow_list: ["."]
+      - type: shell
+    instruction: |
+      ARTIFACT HABITS: Use root's literal repo-relative paths under artifacts/.
+      Preserve prior evidence; sanitize logs; never store secrets. Before stopping,
