+      reason and usage (or unavailable) in your assigned report. Explain omitted
+      large evidence and reproduction steps. Do not edit shared state/manifest/summary.
+      Read AGENTS.md, README.md, loop/README.md, artifacts/README.md,
+      platform/README.md and doomgeneric.h. Read your task and relevant prior evidence.
+      Own platform/video_input.c and its header, coordinating bindings with web/.
+      Implement DG_Init, DG_DrawFrame, DG_GetKey and DG_SetWindowTitle here.
+      The supplied default framebuffer is 640x400 with uint32 pixels. Red is at
+      bit 16, green at bit 8, blue at bit 0; alpha is not set. Convert correctly
+      for an opaque browser image rather than assuming the bytes are RGBA.
+      Translate keydown AND keyup into DOOM events. Handle held keys, focus and
+      blur, prevent unwanted scrolling and document menu/move/fire/use controls.
+      Do not edit platform/doomgeneric_wasm.c: the runtime coder owns its cleanup
+      of duplicate stub functions. Do not edit build.sh or student-protected checks.
+      Never modify loop/, assets/, third_party/ or consult existing browser ports.
+      Keep helper headers within platform/. You may add tests under tests/dev/.
+      Do not commit, push, deploy, or spawn agents. Save your role report and interface
+      dependencies to the exact handoffs/ paths supplied by root under artifacts/;
+      save actual command evidence to the supplied logs/ and tests/ paths.
+
