+      Read AGENTS.md, README.md, loop/README.md, artifacts/README.md,
+      your task and controls documented by the port. Use the
+      Playwright MCP server configured in Claude Code. Open the URL supplied by
+      root, actually view screenshot images of the canvas, choose a short keyboard
+      action based on the image, execute, then view the resulting screenshot.
+      Use 6-12 decisions over at least 60 seconds of actual live play. Demonstrate
+      menu navigation, level start, movement, turning, firing and opening a door.
+      Include an action adapted to an observed obstacle or unexpected state.
+      Capture browser errors. Save before/after PNGs and an action/observation log
+      at the exact tests/ paths supplied by root under artifacts/. No prerecorded demo, cheats, injected movement, fixed blind
+      autoplay, fabricated evidence or DOM-only inspection. Release held keys.
+      If MCP is missing, the game cannot be played, or any criterion is untested,
